    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d708">

                <pb facs="1427" n="1387" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg1387"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">120.280/10–2653: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 708<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in
                        Israel</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d708-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-10-26T19:46:00-05:00">October 26, 1953—7:46
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>328. At dinner with Malik October 24 Secretary had opportunity exchange personal
                    views NE situation with guests including Hassouna, FonMin Bakr of Iraq, Amb
                    Hussein of Egypt, and Chala and Boustani of Lebanon.</p>
                <p>Arabs raised issue Johnston connection American Christian Palestine Committee,
                    stating his selection most unfortunate. Malik said his mission hopeless and he
                    should be recalled gracefully. Secretary’s prompt rejoinder was to effect
                    Johnston enjoyed complete confidence President and State Department; he is
                    considered impartial and able man; and that Arabs would render position
                    untenable in US of those seeking to help them if Johnston rebuffed on present
                    mission. Reference was made to Iraq’s statement that govt would not issue visa.
                    (Bakr said he had made no recommendation this regard.) Egyptian injected note of
                    moderation explaining Egypt’s wish receive any envoy of President and stating
                    Johnston already invited visit Fawzi.</p>
                <p>Chala and Boustani stated they could not even publicly admit having read TVA
                    report in light current political situation. When purposes and nature of desk
                    study were explained their attitude changed.</p>
                <p>Believe conversation generally helpful in producing better understanding on part
                    those present.</p>
                <p>During his talk with Hassouna today President spoke of his interest in Johnston
                    Mission and importance cooperation for Jordan Valley Development.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d708-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d708-f1-content">
                <p>Sent also priority to Amman, Damascus, Beirut, Cairo (for Johnston), Baghdad,
                    Jidda, and New York.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
